# Chaos: shader params and the part rectangle for outfit shaders (O563; client/BASE.md "0200"; src/client/outfit.h/.cpp, luavaluecasts_client.cpp, luafunctions_client.cpp, src/framework/graphics/paintershaderprogram.h/.cpp; after 0001-0199).
# The kill dissolve (overlay module game_killdissolve) draws a dying monster's own sprite through an outfit shader that has to
# know two things an outfit shader never had: how far the dissolve is (per creature, changing every frame) and where the sprite
# is inside the texture atlas (the shader needs a local 0..1 position: top first, from the edges, towards the middle).
#  * Outfit: four floats m_shaderParams (setShaderParams / setShaderParam / getShaderParam, default 0). The Lua outfit table
#    takes them as fields shaderA .. shaderD (absent = 0), so Creature:setOutfit / UICreature:setOutfit carry them like the shader name.
#  * Outfit::draw hands them to the two DrawQueueItemOutfitWithShader it queues (new last constructor argument, default 0).
#  * DrawQueueItemOutfitWithShader::draw: only when one of the four is not 0, shader->setParams(a, b, c, d) (u_Params, the uniform of
#    base patch 0044) and the new shader->setSrc(left, top, width, height) (u_Src, SRC_UNIFORM 19) of the part's rectangle in the texture,
#    in the pixels of a_TexCoord (the same in the framebuffer path of a scaled draw). Every other outfit shader makes no uniform call.
#  * PainterShaderProgram: SRC_UNIFORM 19 bound to "u_Src" in setupUniforms, setSrc. A program that does not declare u_Src ignores it.
#  * Creature.hasShaderParams() (static, true): the capability check of the overlay (an older client build without this patch gets the plain
#    kill effect instead of a dissolve that would never move).
# Cost: nothing for outfits without params (four float compares per shaded part).
# Checked: applies after 0001-0199 on the base tree; the touched .cpp files pass g++ -std=c++17 -fsyntax-only.
# Not built, linked or run in a client; goes live with the next client build.
